  "body": "## What to build\n\nPersist user component libraries on disk, save document components and assembly links in `.camproj` and `.camtools`, and add explicit undoable library sync.\n\n1. Add a user component library store in `crates/app/src/component_library/` (matching `crates/app/src/fixture_library/store.rs`):\n   - Format: `camcraft-components/1` JSON envelope (`units: \"mm\"`), strict all-or-nothing validation naming the offending entry.\n   - Location: `CAMCRAFT_COMPONENTS` env override, else `<platform data dir>/camcraft/components/components.camcomponents`.\n   - Atomic temp-file-then-rename saves.\n   - Project built-in holders (`camcraft_tools::holder_library`) and starter catalog tools as read-only built-in components.\n2. Extend `.camproj` (`crates/app/src/project/`) with a top-level `components` table and an optional `assembly` field on `ToolDto`:\n   - Bump `PROJECT_VERSION` by one step (past PR #2092's v70) so older builds refuse files carrying assemblies instead of judging a fallback cylinder.\n   - Store optional `library_ref { id, content_hash }` on each document component so projects open portably on any machine without silently shifting posted G-code.\n   - Keep pre-assembly `.camproj` files and PR #2092 `holder` references loading unchanged.\n3. Extend `.camtools` (`crates/app/src/tool_library.rs`) to v5 when exporting tools with components or assemblies, keeping v1–v4 unchanged for plain tools.\n4. Add `SyncDocumentComponent` (undoable command) and sync status inspection (`UpToDate`, `UpdateAvailable`, `MissingFromLibrary`) so users explicitly pull user-library edits into a document and re-resolve all referencing assemblies.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Depends on the document component and commands sub-issue of #2452.\n- Requires a `docs/decisions/` entry and `feat!:` / `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer for the project and `.camtools` version bumps.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Round-trip tests pin `components.camcomponents`, `.camproj`, and `.camtools` save and load with byte-stable component definitions and identical derived collision geometry.\n- Tests prove older `.camproj` and `.camtools` files load unchanged.\n- Tests prove corrupt or incompatible component links refuse the file by name.\n- Tests prove `SyncDocumentComponent` pulls an updated user-library component into a project, updates all referencing assemblies, marks operations `Stale`, and undoes cleanly.\n\nPart of #2452\n",
